"# Environment Variables and Compiler Options Reference\n"
"\n"
"## Environment Variables\n"
"\n"
"| Variable | Description |\n"
"| :--- | :--- |\n"
"| `CC` | C compiler command |\n"
"| `CFLAGS` | C compiler flags |\n"
"| `LDFLAGS` | linker flags, e.g. `-L<lib dir>` if you have installed the library in a non-standard directory `lib dir` |\n"
"| `LIBS` | library flags, e.g. `-l<lib>` if you have installed the library in a non-standard directory `lib` |\n"
"\n"
"## Compiler Options\n"
"\n"
"| Option | Description |\n"
"| :--- | :--- |\n"
"| `-x c` | Force the language of the following input files to C |\n"
"| `-x c++` | Force the language of the following input files to C++ |\n"
"| `-x none` | Turn off the effect of any language forcing option, allowing subsequent files to be handled according to their file suffix |\n"
"| `-c` | Compile or assemble the source files, but do not link |\n"
"| `-S` | Compile but do not assemble |\n"
"| `-E` | Only run the C preprocessor |\n"
"| `-o file` | Place the output in file `file` |\n"
"| `-I dir` | Add the directory `dir` to the list of directories to be searched for header files |\n"
"| `-L dir` | Add the directory `dir` to the list of directories to be searched for `-l` |\n"
"| `-l library` | Search for a library named `library` when linking |\n"
"| `-static` | On systems that support dynamic linking, this prevents linking with shared libraries |\n"
"| `-shared` | Produce a shared object which can then be linked with other objects to form an executable |\n"
"| `-g` | Produce debugging information in the operating system's native format |\n"
"| `-ggdb` | Produce debugging information for use by GDB |\n"
"| `-O0` | Reduce compilation time and make debugging produce the expected results |\n"
"| `-O1` | Reduce code size and execution time, without performing any optimizations that take a great deal of compilation time |\n"
"| `-O2` | Optimize even more. GCC performs nearly all supported optimizations that do not involve a space-speed tradeoff |\n"
"| `-O3` | Optimize even more. Enables all optimizations specified by `-O2` and also turns on the `-finline-functions` and `-funswitch-loops` options |\n"
"| `-Os` | Optimize for size. Enables all `-O2` optimizations that do not typically increase code size. It also performs further optimizations designed to reduce code size |\n"
"| `-fno-inline` | Do not pay attention to the `inline` keyword |\n"
"| `-pthread` | Define additional macros required by the POSIX threads library |\n"
"| `-Wall` | Enable all warnings about constructions that some users consider questionable, and that are easy to avoid (or modify to prevent the warning), even in conjunction with macros |\n"
"| `-Werror` | Make all warnings into errors |\n"
"| `-Wno-unused-result` | Do not warn if a caller of a function marked with attribute `warn_unused_result` does not use its return value |\n"
"| `-fopenmp` | Enable handling of OpenMP directives `#pragma omp` in C/C++ |\n"
"| `-m32` | Generate code for a 32-bit environment |\n"
"| `-m64` | Generate code for a 64-bit environment |\n"
"| `-march=native` | Specify the architecture of the local machine |\n"
"| `-mtune=native` | Tune the generated code for the local machine |\n"
"| `-fPIC` | Generate position-independent code (PIC) suitable for use in a shared library |\n"
"| `-fpic` | Generate position-independent code (PIC) suitable for use in a shared library, if supported for the target machine |\n"
"| `-fpie` | Generate position-independent code (PIC) suitable for use in a pie (position independent executable) |\n"
"| `-fPIE` | Generate position-independent code (PIC) suitable for use in a pie (position independent executable), if supported for the target machine |\n"
"| `-fstack-protector` | Emit extra code to check for buffer overflows, such as stack smashing attacks |\n"
"| `-fstack-protector-all` | Like `-fstack-protector` except that it protects all functions |\n"
"| `-fstack-protector-strong` | Like `-fstack-protector` but includes additional functions to be protected — those that have local array definitions, or have references to local frame addresses |\n"
"| `-fno-stack-protector` | Disable stack protection |\n"
"| `-D name` | Predefine `name` as a macro, with definition `1` |\n"
"| `-D name=definition` | The contents of the `definition` are tokenized and processed as if they appeared during translation phase three in a `#define` directive |\n"
"| `-U name` | Cancel any previous definition of `name`, either built in or provided with a `-D` option |\n"
"| `-include file` | Process `file` as if `#include \"file\"` appeared as the first line of the primary source file |\n"
"| `-imacros file` | Exactly like `-include`, except that any output produced by scanning `file` is thrown away |\n"
"| `-idirafter dir` | Add the directory `dir` to the second include chain |\n"
"| `-iprefix prefix` | Specify `prefix` as the prefix for subsequent `-iwithprefix` options |\n"
"| `-iwithprefix dir` | Add a directory to the second include chain |\n"
"| `-iwithprefixbefore dir` | Add a directory to the main include chain |\n"
"| `-isystem dir` | Add the directory `dir` to the head of the second include chain |\n"
"| `-iquote dir` | Add the directory `dir` to the list of directories to be searched for header files, for the case where `#include \"file\"` is used |\n"
"| `-nostdinc` | Do not search the standard system directories for header files |\n"
"| `-nostdinc++` | Do not search for header files in the standard directories specific to C++, but do still search the standard directories valid for C |\n"
"| `-nostdlib` | Do not use the standard system startup files or libraries when linking |\n"
"| `-nodefaultlibs` | Do not use the standard system libraries when linking |\n"
"| `-Wl,option` | Pass `option` as an option to the linker |\n"
"| `-Xlinker option` | Pass `option` as an option to the linker |\n"
"| `-u symbol` | Pretend the symbol `symbol` is undefined, to force linking of library modules to define it |\n"
"| `-z keyword` | Pass the `-z` option to the linker |\n"
"| `-rdynamic` | Pass the `-export-dynamic` option to the ELF linker, which instructs the linker to add all symbols to the dynamic symbol table |\n"
"| `-s` | Remove all symbol table and relocation information from the executable |\n"
"| `-v` | Print the commands executed to run the stages of compilation |\n"
"| `-###` | Like `-v` except the commands are not executed |\n"
"| `-pipe` | Use pipes rather than temporary files for communication between the various stages of compilation |\n"
"| `-time` | Report the CPU time taken by each subprocess in the compilation sequence |\n"
"| `-wrapper` | Invoke all subcommands under a wrapper program |\n"
"| `-fno-omit-frame-pointer` | Do not omit the frame pointer in functions that do not need one |\n"
"| `-fomit-frame-pointer` | Omit the frame pointer in functions that do not need one |\n"
"| `-fno-strict-aliasing` | Disable optimizations that depend on strict aliasing rules |\n"
"| `-fstrict-aliasing` | Allow the compiler to assume the strictest aliasing rules applicable to the language being compiled |\n"
"| `-fno-exceptions` | Disable exception handling |\n"
"| `-fexceptions` | Enable exception handling |\n"
"| `-fno-rtti` | Disable generation of information about every class with virtual functions for use by the C++ runtime type identification features (`dynamic_cast` and `typeid`) |\n"
"| `-frtti` | Enable generation of information about every class with virtual functions for use by the C++ runtime type identification features (`dynamic_cast` and `typeid`) |\n"
"| `-fno-threadsafe-statics` | Do not emit the extra code to use the routines specified in the C++ ABI for thread-safe initialization of local statics |\n"
"| `-fthreadsafe-statics` | Emit the extra code to use the routines specified in the C++ ABI for thread-safe initialization of local statics |\n"
"| `-fno-strict-overflow` | Disable optimizations that assume that signed overflow does not occur |\n"
"| `-fstrict-overflow` | Allow the compiler to assume that signed overflow does not occur |\n"
"| `-fno-wrapv` | Disable optimizations that assume that signed overflow does not wrap around |\n"
"| `-fwrapv` | Assume that signed arithmetic overflow wraps around |\n"
"| `-fno-trapv` | Disable generation of traps for signed overflow on addition, subtraction, multiplication operations |\n"
"| `-ftrapv` | Generate traps for signed overflow on addition, subtraction, multiplication operations |\n"
"| `-fno-builtin` | Do not recognize built-in functions that do not begin with `__builtin_` as prefix |\n"
"| `-fbuiltin` | Recognize built-in functions that do not begin with `__builtin_` as prefix |\n"
"| `-fno-asm` | Do not recognize `asm`, `inline` or `typeof` as keywords |\n"
"| `-fasm` | Recognize `asm`, `inline` or `typeof` as keywords |\n"
"| `-fno-gnu89-inline` | Use the `inline` keyword semantics specified in the C99 standard |\n"
"| `-fgnu89-inline` | Use the GNU89 `inline` keyword semantics |\n"
"| `-fno-ms-extensions` | Disable some Microsoft extensions |\n"
"| `-fms-extensions` | Accept some non-standard constructs used in Microsoft header files |\n"
"| `-fno-ms-compatibility` | Disable Microsoft compatibility |\n"
"| `-fms-compatibility` | Accept some non-standard constructs used in Microsoft header files |\n"
"| `-fno-ms-compat-version` | Disable Microsoft compatibility version |\n"
"| `-fms-compat-version` | Set the Microsoft compatibility version |\n"
"| `-fno-delayed-branch` | Disable delayed branch optimization |\n"
"| `-fdelayed-branch` | Enable delayed branch optimization |\n"
"| `-fno-guess-branch-probability` | Disable guessing branch probabilities |\n"
"| `-fguess-branch-probability` | Enable guessing branch probabilities |\n"
"| `-fno-reorder-blocks` | Disable reordering basic blocks |\n"
"| `-freorder-blocks` | Enable reordering basic blocks |\n"
"| `-fno-reorder-blocks-and-partition` | Disable reordering basic blocks and partitioning |\n"
"| `-freorder-blocks-and-partition` | Enable reordering basic blocks and partitioning |\n"
"| `-fno-reorder-functions` | Disable reordering functions |\n"
"| `-freorder-functions` | Enable reordering functions |\n"
"| `-fno-tree-vectorize` | Disable vectorization of loops |\n"
"| `-ftree-vectorize` | Enable vectorization of loops |\n"
"| `-fno-tree-loop-vectorize` | Disable vectorization of loops |\n"
"| `-ftree-loop-vectorize` | Enable vectorization of loops |\n"
"| `-fno-tree-slp-vectorize` | Disable vectorization of straight-line code |\n"
"| `-ftree-slp-vectorize` | Enable vectorization of straight-line code |\n"
"| `-fno-vect-cost-model` | Disable the vectorizer cost model |\n"
"| `-fvect-cost-model` | Enable the vectorizer cost model |\n"
"| `-fno-tree-pre` | Disable the PRE (partial redundancy elimination) optimization |\n"
"| `-ftree-pre` | Enable the PRE (partial redundancy elimination) optimization |\n"
"| `-fno-tree-fre` | Disable the FRE (full redundancy elimination) optimization |\n"
"| `-ftree-fre` | Enable the FRE (full redundancy elimination) optimization |\n"
"| `-fno-tree-dominator-opts` | Disable dominator-based optimizations |\n"
"| `-ftree-dominator-opts` | Enable dominator-based optimizations |\n"
"| `-fno-tree-sra` | Disable scalar replacement of aggregates |\n"
"| `-ftree-sra` | Enable scalar replacement of aggregates |\n"
"| `-fno-tree-ter` | Disable temporary expression replacement |\n"
"| `-ftree-ter` | Enable temporary expression replacement |\n"
"| `-fno-tree-sink` | Disable sinking of expressions |\n"
"| `-ftree-sink` | Enable sinking of expressions |\n"
"| `-fno-tree-loop-im` | Disable loop invariant motion |\n"
"| `-ftree-loop-im` | Enable loop invariant motion |\n"
"| `-fno-tree-loop-distribution` | Disable loop distribution |\n"
"| `-ftree-loop-distribution` | Enable loop distribution |\n"
